.Dt INDEXING 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm indexing
.Nd indexing dan hashing, dari B+ tree sampai bitmap
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Ini catatan Chapter 11 dari buku Database System Concepts. Isinya:
basic concepts, ordered indices, B+ tree, B tree, static hashing,
dynamic hashing, comparison, index definition in SQL, multiple-key
access.
.Pp
Bahasa santai. Tiap konsep dijelasin kenapa dia ada. Karena
indexing itu yang bikin query cepet. Tanpa index, database
harus scan semua baris tiap query.
.Ss Bagian 1: Basic Concepts
.Sy Index
= mekanisme buat speed up access ke data.
.Pp
.Sy Search key
= atribut (atau set atribut) yang dipakai buat lookup record.
.Pp
.Sy Index file
= file yang berisi record (disebut index entry) dengan bentuk:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
search-key    pointer
.Ed
.Sy Index file
biasanya jauh lebih kecil dari file aslinya.
.Pp
.Sy Dua jenis index:
.Bl -tag -width "Hash indices" -offset indent
.It Sy Ordered indices
Search key disimpen in sorted order.
.It Sy Hash indices
Search key didistribusi uniformly across bucket pakai hash
function.
.El
.Ss Bagian 1.1: Metrik Evaluasi
.Bl -tag -width "Space overhead" -offset indent
.It Sy Access types
Records dengan nilai tertentu, atau range nilai.
.It Sy Access time
.It Sy Insertion time
.It Sy Deletion time
.It Sy Space overhead
.El
.Ss Bagian 2: Ordered Indices
.Sy Index entry disimpen sorted berdasarkan search key.
.Ss Bagian 2.1: Primary vs Secondary Index
.Bl -tag -width "Secondary" -offset indent
.It Sy Primary index
Index yang search key-nya nentuin sequential order file.
Disebut juga clustering index.
.It Sy Secondary index
Index yang search key-nya beda dari sequential order file.
Disebut juga non-clustering index.
.It Sy Index-sequential file
Ordered sequential file dengan primary index.
.El
.Ss Bagian 2.2: Dense Index
.Sy Dense index
= index record muncul buat setiap search-key value di file.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh:
Index di ID attribute.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
10101 --> record ID 10101
12121 --> record ID 12121
15151 --> record ID 15151
...
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 2.3: Sparse Index
.Sy Sparse index
= index record cuma buat beberapa search-key value.
.Pp
.Sy Syarat:
Records harus sequentially ordered di search key.
.Pp
.Sy Cara locate record dengan search-key K:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Cari index record dengan search-key terbesar < K.
.It
Search file sequentially mulai dari record yang ditunjuk.
.El
.Ss Bagian 2.4: Dense vs Sparse
.Bl -tag -width "Sparse" -offset indent
.It Sy Dense
Space lebih besar, maintenance overhead lebih besar, tapi
locate record lebih cepet.
.It Sy Sparse
Space dan maintenance lebih kecil, tapi locate lebih lambat.
.El
.Sy Trade-off bagus:
Sparse index dengan index entry buat setiap block di file,
corresponding ke least search-key value di block.
.Ss Bagian 2.5: Secondary Index
.Sy Index record point ke bucket yang contains pointer ke semua
actual record dengan search-key value tertentu.
.Pp
.Sy Secondary index harus dense.
Karena kalau sparse, record dengan nilai tertentu bisa
tersebar di banyak block.
.Ss Bagian 2.6: Update Index
.Sy Kapan file dimodif, setiap index di file harus diupdate.
.Pp
.Sy Sequential scan pakai primary index:
Efficient.
.Sy Sequential scan pakai secondary index:
Expensive. Tiap record access mungkin fetch new block dari disk.
Block fetch 5-10 ms vs memory access ~100 ns.
.Ss Bagian 2.7: Multilevel Index
.Sy Masalah:
Kalau primary index nggak fit di memory, access jadi mahal.
.Pp
.Sy Solusi:
Treat primary index sebagai sequential file, construct sparse
index di atasnya.
.Bl -tag -width "Inner index" -offset indent
.It Sy Outer index
Sparse index dari primary index.
.It Sy Inner index
Primary index file.
.El
.Sy Kalau outer index masih kekecilan:
Buat level index lagi, dst.
.Ss Bagian 2.8: Deletion
.Bl -tag -width "Sparse" -offset indent
.It Sy Dense index
Deletion search-key similar ke file record deletion.
.It Sy Sparse index
Kalau entry search-key ada di index, delete dengan replace
entry dengan next search-key value di file.
Kalau next search-key value udah punya index entry, delete
entry-nya instead.
.El
.Ss Bagian 2.9: Insertion
.Bl -tag -width "Sparse" -offset indent
.It Sy Dense index
Kalau search-key value nggak muncul di index, insert.
.It Sy Sparse index
Kalau index stores entry per block, no change kecuali ada
new block. Kalau new block dibuat, insert first search-key
value di new block.
.El
.Ss Bagian 3: B+ Tree Index Files
.Sy B+ tree
= alternatif dari indexed-sequential files.
.Pp
.Sy Kelemahan indexed-sequential files:
Performance degrade seiring file grows. Banyak overflow block.
Periodic reorganization diperlukan.
.Pp
.Sy Keunggulan B+ tree:
Automatically reorganize dengan small, local changes.
Reorganization of entire file nggak perlu.
.Pp
.Sy Kelemahan B+ tree:
Extra insertion dan deletion overhead, space overhead.
.Sy Tapi advantages outweigh disadvantages.
B+ tree extensively used.
.Ss Bagian 3.1: Properti B+ Tree
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Semua path dari root ke leaf sama panjang.
.It
Node non-root non-leaf punya antara
.Sy ceil(n/2)
dan
.Sy n
children.
.It
Leaf node punya antara
.Sy ceil((n-1)/2)
dan
.Sy n-1
values.
.It
Kalau root bukan leaf, punya minimal 2 children.
.It
Kalau root leaf, punya antara 0 dan n-1 values.
.El
.Ss Bagian 3.2: Typical Node
.Bd -literal -offset indent
P1  K1  P2  K2  ...  Pn-1  Kn-1  Pn
.Ed
.Sy K
= search key values.
.Sy P
= pointer ke children (non-leaf) atau pointer ke record/
bucket (leaf).
.Pp
.Sy Search keys in a node are ordered:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
K1 < K2 < K3 < ... < Kn-1
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 3.3: Leaf Node
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Pointer Pi point ke file record dengan search-key Ki.
.It
Kalau Li dan Lj leaf nodes dan i < j, search-key values
di Li <= di Lj.
.It
Pn point ke next leaf node in search-key order.
.El
.Ss Bagian 3.4: Non-Leaf Node
.Sy Form a multi-level sparse index on leaf nodes.
.Pp
.Sy Untuk non-leaf node dengan m pointer:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Semua search-key di subtree P1 < K1.
.It
Untuk 2 <= i <= n-1, semua search-key di subtree Pi >= Ki-1
dan < Ki.
.It
Semua search-key di subtree Pn >= Kn-1.
.El
.Ss Bagian 3.5: Contoh B+ Tree
.Bd -literal -offset indent
                 [El Said | Mozart]
                /        |        \
               /         |         \
    [Brandt|Califieri|  [El Said|Gold|  [Mozart|Singh|
     Crick|Einstein]     Katz|Kim]       Srinivasan|Wu]
.Ed
.Sy n = 6:
Leaf nodes: 3-5 values. Non-leaf: 3-6 children. Root: >= 2 children.
.Ss Bagian 3.6: Kenapa B+ Tree Cepet
.Sy Jumlah level:
B+ tree contains relatively small number of levels.
.Sy Contoh:
1 juta search key value, n = 100 \(-> height <= log_50(1,000,000) = 4.
Compare dengan binary tree: ~20 node access.
.Pp
.Sy Kenapa penting?
Karena setiap node access butuh disk I/O, ~20 ms.
.Ss Bagian 3.7: Insertion
.Sy Algoritma:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Cari leaf node di mana search-key value bakal muncul.
.It
Kalau search-key value udah ada:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Add record ke file.
.It
Kalau perlu, add pointer ke bucket.
.El
.It
Kalau search-key value belum ada:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Add record ke main file (bikin bucket kalau perlu).
.It
Kalau ada room di leaf, insert (key, pointer) pair.
.It
Kalau nggak, split node.
.El
.El
.Ss Bagian 3.8: Splitting Leaf Node
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Ambil n (key, pointer) pairs (termasuk yang baru) in sorted order.
.It
Place first ceil(n/2) di original node, sisanya di new node.
.It
Insert (k, p) di parent node.
.It
Kalau parent full, split dan propagate up.
.El
.Sy Worst case:
Root node split, height naik 1.
.Ss Bagian 3.9: Splitting Non-Leaf Node
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Copy N ke memory area M dengan space n+1 pointer dan n keys.
.It
Insert (k, p) ke M.
.It
Copy P1, K1, ..., K_[n/2]-1, P_[n/2] dari M back ke node N.
.It
Copy P_[n/2+1], ..., Pn+1 dari M ke new node N'.
.It
Insert (K_[n/2], N') ke parent N.
.El
.Ss Bagian 3.10: Deletion
.Sy Algoritma:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Cari record yang di-delete, remove dari main file dan bucket.
.It
Remove (search-key value, pointer) dari leaf node.
.It
Kalau node terlalu sedikit entries dan entries di node +
sibling fit di single node, merge siblings:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Insert semua search-key value di dua node ke single node
(yang kiri), delete node lain.
.It
Delete pair (Ki-1, Pi) dari parent, recursively.
.El
.It
Kalau nggak bisa merge, redistribute pointers:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Redistribute pointer antara node dan sibling.
.It
Update corresponding search-key value di parent.
.El
.El
.Sy Cascade:
Node deletions bisa cascade upwards sampai node dengan
.Sy ceil(n/2)
atau lebih pointer ditemukan.
.Pp
.Sy Root node:
Kalau root cuma punya 1 pointer setelah deletion, delete dan
sole child jadi root.
.Ss Bagian 3.11: Duplicate Search Keys
.Sy Masalah:
Kalau ada duplicate search key, nggak bisa guarantee
K1 < K2 < ... < Kn-1.
Tapi bisa guarantee K1 <= K2 <= ... <= Kn-1.
.Pp
.Sy Handling:
Traverse Pi even if V = Ki. As soon as reach leaf C, check
if C punya search key values less than V. Kalau iya, set
C = right sibling. Traverse consecutive leaves buat temuin
all occurrences.
.Ss Bagian 3.12: B+ Tree File Organization
.Sy Data file degradation problem
solved dengan B+ tree file organization.
.Pp
.Sy Leaf nodes
simpen records, bukan pointers.
.Pp
.Sy Kelemahan:
Records lebih besar dari pointers. Max records per leaf node
lebih sedikit dari max pointers di non-leaf node.
.Pp
.Sy Space utilization:
Good space utilization penting. Involve more sibling nodes
in redistribution during splits/merges.
.Ss Bagian 4: B Tree Index Files
.Sy B tree
= similar ke B+ tree, tapi search key values muncul hanya
sekali. Eliminate redundant storage.
.Pp
.Sy Non-leaf nodes:
Search key muncul nowhere else. Additional pointer field
buat each search key.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
P1  B1  K1  P2  B2  K2  ...  Pm-1  Bm-1  Km-1  Pm
.Ed
.Sy Bi
= bucket atau file record pointer.
.Ss Bagian 4.1: B Tree vs B+ Tree
.Bl -tag -width "Kelebihan B Tree" -offset indent
.It Sy Kelebihan B Tree
May use fewer tree nodes. Sometimes find search-key value
before reaching leaf node.
.It Sy Kelemahan B Tree
Only small fraction search-key values found early. Non-leaf
nodes larger, fan-out reduced. Typically greater depth.
Insertion/deletion more complicated. Implementation harder.
.El
.Sy Kesimpulan:
Typically, advantages of B Tree nggak outweigh disadvantages.
.Ss Bagian 5: Hashing
.Ss Bagian 5.1: Bucket
.Sy Bucket
= unit of storage containing one or more records
(typically a disk block).
.Pp
.Sy Hash file organization:
Bucket of record didapat langsung dari search-key value pakai
hash function.
.Pp
.Sy Hash function h:
Fungsi dari set search-key values K ke set bucket addresses B.
.Pp
.Sy Kenapa perlu hash?
Buat locate record cepet, insertion, deletion. Records dengan
search-key value berbeda bisa map ke bucket yang sama,
jadi bucket harus di-search sequentially.
.Ss Bagian 5.2: Hash Function
.Sy Worst hash function:
Map semua search-key values ke bucket yang sama.
.Sy Ideal hash function:
Uniform (setiap bucket punya jumlah search-key value sama)
dan random.
.Ss Bagian 5.3: Bucket Overflow
.Sy Penyebab:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Insufficient buckets.
.It
Skew in distribution of records.
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Multiple records punya same search-key value.
.It
Chosen hash function produces non-uniform distribution.
.El
.El
.Sy Handling:
.Bl -tag -width "Open hashing" -offset indent
.It Sy Overflow chaining (closed hashing)
Overflow buckets dari given bucket di-chain in linked list.
.It Sy Open hashing
Nggak pakai overflow buckets. Nggak suitable buat database.
.El
.Ss Bagian 5.4: Hash Indices
.Sy Hash index
= organize search keys dengan associated record pointers ke
hash file structure.
.Pp
.Sy Strictly speaking:
Hash indices are always secondary indices.
.Sy Kalau file itself organized using hashing:
Separate primary hash index nggak perlu.
.Ss Bagian 6: Static Hashing
.Sy Static hashing:
Hash function h map search-key values ke fixed set B of
bucket addresses.
.Pp
.Sy Masalah:
Database grow atau shrink seiring waktu.
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Kalau initial number of buckets kekecilan dan file grows,
performance degrade karena too much overflows.
.It
Kalau space dialokasi buat anticipated growth, significant
amount of space wasted initially.
.It
Kalau database shrinks, space wasted lagi.
.El
.Sy Solusi:
Periodic reorganization dengan new hash function. Expensive,
disrupts operations.
.Sy Better solution:
Allow number of buckets dimodif dynamically.
.Ss Bagian 7: Dynamic Hashing
.Sy Good for database yang grows and shrinks.
.Ss Bagian 7.1: Extendable Hashing
.Sy Ide:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Hash function generates values over large range (b-bit, b=32).
.It
At any time, use only prefix dari hash function buat index
ke bucket address table.
.It
Length of prefix = i bit, 0 <= i <= 32.
.It
Bucket address table size = 2^i.
.It
i grows and shrinks as database grows and shrinks.
.It
Multiple entries di bucket address table bisa point ke bucket
yang sama.
.It
Actual number of buckets < 2^i.
.El
.Ss Bagian 7.2: Operasi Extendable Hashing
.Sy Setiap bucket j stores value ij:
Semua entries yang point ke bucket sama punya value sama
di first ij bits.
.Pp
.Sy Locate bucket containing search-key Kj:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Compute h(Kj) = X.
.It
Use first i high order bits of X as displacement ke bucket
address table.
.It
Follow pointer ke appropriate bucket.
.El
.Ss Bagian 7.3: Insertion Extendable Hashing
.Sy Algoritma:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Follow same procedure as lookup, locate bucket j.
.It
Kalau ada room, insert record.
.It
Kalau nggak, split bucket dan insertion re-attempted.
.El
.Sy Split bucket j:
.Bl -tag -width "i = ij" -offset indent
.It Sy Kalau i > ij (lebih dari satu pointer ke bucket j):
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Allocate new bucket z, set ij = iz = (ij + 1).
.It
Update second half of bucket address table entries original
pointing ke j, point ke z.
.It
Remove each record dari bucket j, reinsert (di j atau z).
.It
Recompute new bucket for Kj dan insert.
.El
.It Sy Kalau i = ij (cuma satu pointer ke bucket j):
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Kalau i reaches limit b atau too many splits, create overflow
bucket.
.It
Else, increment i dan double size of bucket address table.
.It
Replace each entry dengan dua entry yang point ke bucket
yang sama.
.It
Recompute new bucket address table entry for Kj.
.It
Now i > ij, use first case.
.El
.El
.Ss Bagian 7.4: Deletion Extendable Hashing
.Sy Algoritma:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Locate key di bucket, remove.
.It
Bucket bisa di-remove kalau empty.
.It
Coalescing of buckets bisa dilakukan (cuma dengan "buddy"
bucket having same ij dan same ij-1 prefix).
.It
Decreasing bucket address table size juga possible.
.Sy Note:
Decreasing bucket address table size expensive, lakukan
cuma kalau number of buckets much smaller than table size.
.El
.Ss Bagian 7.5: Benefit dan Disadvantage
.Bl -tag -width "Disadvantages" -offset indent
.It Sy Benefits
Hash performance nggak degrade dengan growth of file.
Minimal space overhead.
.It Sy Disadvantages
Extra level of indirection.
Bucket address table may become very big.
Cannot allocate very large contiguous areas on disk.
Changing size of bucket address table expensive.
.El
.Sy Alternative:
Linear hashing. Allows incremental growth of directory.
At cost of more bucket overflows.
.Ss Bagian 8: Comparison Ordered Index vs Hashing
.Sy Faktor:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Cost of periodic reorganization.
.It
Relative frequency of insertions and deletions.
.It
Expected type of queries.
.El
.Sy Hashing lebih baik buat:
Retrieve records dengan specified value.
.Sy Ordered indices lebih baik buat:
Range queries.
.Ss Bagian 8.1: Prakteknya
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
PostgreSQL supports hash indices, but discourages use due to
poor performance.
.It
Oracle supports static hash organization, but not hash indices.
.It
SQLServer supports only B+ trees.
.El
.Ss Bagian 9: Bitmap Indices
.Sy Bitmap index
= special type of index designed buat efficient querying on
multiple keys.
.Pp
.Sy Records
in a relation diasumsikan numbered sequentially.
.Pp
.Sy Applicable
on attributes yang take relatively small number distinct values.
Contoh: gender, country, state, income-level.
.Pp
.Sy Bitmap
= array of bits.
.Ss Bagian 9.1: Cara Kerja
.Sy Bitmap index on attribute punya bitmap buat setiap value
dari attribute.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
record  ID      gender  income_level
0       76766   m       L1
1       22222   f       L2
2       12121   f       L1
3       15151   m       L4
4       58583   f       L3

Bitmaps for gender:
  m:  10010
  f:  01101

Bitmaps for income_level:
  L1: 10100
  L2: 01000
  L3: 00001
  L4: 00010
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 9.2: Bitmap Operations
.Sy Queries
answered using bitmap operations:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Intersection (AND)
.It
Union (OR)
.It
Complementation (NOT)
.El
.Sy Contoh:
Males with income level L1:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
10010 AND 10100 = 10000
.Ed
.Sy Counting matching tuples
even faster.
.Ss Bagian 9.3: Space Efficiency
.Sy Bitmap indices
generally very small compared with relation size.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh:
Kalau record 100 byte, space buat single bitmap 1/800 of
relation space.
Kalau number of distinct attribute values 8, bitmap cuma 1%
of relation size.
.Ss Bagian 9.4: Deletion Handling
.Sy Existence bitmap:
Note if there is valid record at record location.
Needed for complementation.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
not(A=v): (NOT bitmap_A_v) AND ExistenceBitmap
.Ed
.Sy SQL null semantics:
Keep bitmaps buat all values, even null.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
NOT(A=v): intersect above result with
           (NOT bitmap_A_Null)
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 9.5: Optimisasi Bitmap
.Sy Bitmaps are packed into words:
Single word and (basic CPU instruction) computes AND of
32 atau 64 bits at once.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh:
1 million-bit maps bisa di-AND dengan cuma 31,250 instruction.
.Pp
.Sy Counting 1s:
Use each byte to index into precomputed array of 256 elements
storing count of 1s.
.Ss Bagian 9.6: Bitmap di B+ Tree
.Sy Bitmaps bisa dipakai instead of Tuple-ID lists
at leaf levels of B+ trees, buat values dengan large number
of matching records.
.Pp
.Sy Worthwhile
kalau >1/64 dari records punya value itu (assuming tuple-id
64 bits).
.Ss Bagian 10: Index Definition in SQL
.Sy Create index:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
create index <index-name> on <relation-name> (<attribute-list>)
.Ed
.Sy Contoh:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
create index b-index on branch(branch_name)
.Ed
.Sy Create unique index:
Indirectly specify dan enforce condition bahwa search key
adalah candidate key.
Nggak really required kalau SQL unique integrity constraint
supported.
.Sy Drop index:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
drop index <index-name>
.Ed
.Sy Most database systems
allow specification of type of index dan clustering.
.Ss Bagian 11: Multiple-Key Access
.Sy Use multiple indices
buat certain types of queries.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
select ID from instructor
where dept_name = "Finance" and salary = 80000
.Ed
.Sy Strategi:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Use index on dept_name, test salary = 80000.
.It
Use index on salary, test dept_name = "Finance".
.It
Use both, intersect pointer sets.
.El
.Ss Bagian 11.1: Composite Search Key
.Sy Composite search key
= search key containing more than one attribute.
Contoh: (dept_name, salary).
.Pp
.Sy Lexicographic ordering:
(a1, a2) < (b1, b2) kalau a1 < b1, atau a1 = b1 dan a2 < b2.
.Ss Bagian 11.2: Index on Multiple Attributes
.Sy Contoh:
Index on (dept_name, salary).
.Bd -literal -offset indent
where dept_name = "Finance" and salary = 80000
.Ed
Index bisa dipakai buat fetch cuma records yang satisfy
kedua conditions.
.Pp
.Sy Separate indices less efficient:
May fetch many records yang satisfy cuma satu condition.
.Pp
.Sy Bisa handle:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
where dept_name = "Finance" and salary < 80000
.Ed
.Sy Nggak bisa handle:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
where dept_name < "Finance" and balance = 80000
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 11.3: Covering Index
.Sy Covering index:
Tambah extra attributes ke index biar query bisa avoid
fetching actual records.
.Pp
.Sy Berguna buat:
Secondary indices.
.Sy Bisa store extra attributes hanya di leaf.
.Ss Bagian 11.4: Hash Values untuk Multiple Attributes
.Sy Hash values split into segments
yang depend ke each attribute of search-key.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh:
n = 2, search-key = (customer-street, customer-city).
.Bd -literal -offset indent
(Main, Harrison)   -> 101 111
(Main, Brooklyn)   -> 101 001
(Park, Palo Alto)  -> 010 010
(Spring, Brooklyn) -> 001 001
(Alma, Palo Alto)  -> 110 010
.Ed
.Sy Equality query on single attribute:
Lookup multiple buckets.
.Ss Bagian 11.5: Grid Files
.Sy Struktur
buat speed up processing general multiple search-key queries
involving one or more comparison operators.
.Pp
.Sy Grid file:
Single grid array dan satu linear scale buat each search-key
attribute.
.Pp
.Sy Multiple cells
of grid array bisa point ke same bucket.
.Pp
.Sy Handling queries:
Bisa handle (a1 <= A <= a2), (b1 <= B <= b2), dan kombinasi
keduanya.
.Ss Ringkasan
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Konsep                Inti
Index                 Speed up access
Search key            Attribute buat lookup
Index entry           (search-key, pointer)
Ordered index         Search key sorted
Hash index            Hash function
Primary index         Search key = sequential order
Secondary index       Search key != sequential order
Dense index           Entry buat setiap value
Sparse index          Entry buat beberapa value
Multilevel index      Index di atas index
B+ tree               Balanced tree, search key di leaf
B tree                Search key muncul sekali
Bucket                Unit storage
Hash function         Map key ke bucket
Overflow chaining     Chain overflow bucket
Static hashing        Fixed number buckets
Extendable hashing    Dynamic number buckets
Bitmap index          Array of bits
Composite search key  Multiple attributes
Covering index        Index dengan extra attributes
Grid file             Multi-dimensional index
.Ed
Kalau kamu cuma inget satu hal dari catatan ini, inget ini:
.Sy index itu trade-off antara space dan speed.
Setiap index bikin query cepet, tapi bikin insert/update/
delete lambat (karena harus update index juga) dan makan
space. Jangan bikin index buat semua kolom. Cuma bikin index
buat kolom yang sering di-query atau di-join.
